## Summary
The article discusses the shift towards remote working, which began before the COVID-19 pandemic and has been further accelerated by pandemic-related directives. It emphasizes the importance of implementing data protection measures, particularly in compliance with GDPR standards, to ensure security in remote work environments.

## Key Points
- Remote working trend was emerging prior to the COVID-19 pandemic.
- Public health directives during the pandemic have increased remote work adoption.
- Data protection is critical for securing sensitive information when working remotely.
- GDPR provides essential guidelines for organizations handling data in remote settings.
- Adaptation of security protocols is necessary for distributed workforces.


